Among the assumptions underlying the above development we focus on three
prominent ones. The first two stem from assumptions of the  basic LR tests described in ((stijnen)), while the third is specific to Bartlett correction.

\begin{enumerate}
  \item The first is correct specification of the likelihood,
in particular, gaussianity of the unobserved random effect. [[we refer
