\subsection{Incidence}

niel-weise ((2008)) also carries out a meta-analysis on the efficiacy
of an anti-infection treatment for catheters. Each of the 9 included
studies reports, for each arm, the number of catheter-related
infections observed in a population as well as the total
``catheter-days'', the sum over the population of the number of days
each subject used a catheter.

We use the poisson-normal model ((ref)) to obtain CIs for the log
incidence rate in each arm, and the binomial-irr model ((ref)) to
obtain a CI for the log-incidence-rate ratio. For this smaller
meta-analysis the difference between the corrected and uncorrected CIs
is more dramatic. These differences include a loss of significance at
the nominal level $\alpha=.05$ for the log-IR ratio study.

